      "message": "@spinler@us.ibm.com It seems that, in Hex Data Word 3, bits 0–2 are used for the Redundant Service Processor Indication. Therefore, I think we should set this field only for a redundant BMC system. If the BMC position is not available, we should leave the field unset, both in redundant and non-redundant BMC systems.\n\nI also assume this code is triggered only for BMC-generated PELs, since this field identifies the SRC originator.\n\nThe old code does not set bits 0–2.",
